WEBVTT

00:00:14.440 --> 00:00:17.080
We would like to have a word with Tatsumi.

00:00:18.170 --> 00:00:21.330
Team's formation... Game instructions...

00:00:21.610 --> 00:00:23.080
Don't screw with us!

00:00:23.080 --> 00:00:25.550
What are you doing to our ETU?!

00:00:25.550 --> 00:00:27.330
Get your ass down here, Tatsumi!

00:00:28.130 --> 00:00:30.630
Manager, do you need me to take care of them?

00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:33.380
I should be able to-

00:00:33.640 --> 00:00:34.700
Let me ask...

00:00:35.540 --> 00:00:38.230
Am I the one they wanna have a word with?

00:00:39.210 --> 00:00:41.050
Alright then, I'll just have to go see them.

00:00:44.920 --> 00:00:46.820
I wouldn't want you to get involved.

00:00:47.650 --> 00:00:50.610
Dealing with the fans is also part of my job.

00:00:51.240 --> 00:00:54.890
You people just need to concentrate on football.

00:00:56.030 --> 00:00:57.040
Got it?

00:01:01.750 --> 00:01:03.730
I can't let you out.

00:01:04.390 --> 00:01:07.430
I will do it. I will convince them, even if I have to do it all night!

00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:09.240
This is my job.

00:01:17.420 --> 00:01:19.830
Amazing!

00:01:30.230 --> 00:01:31.690
Are they gods?

00:01:32.870 --> 00:01:34.040
Pass it, Pepe!

00:01:44.410 --> 00:01:47.390
If they are not going to win today, I'll really be a laughing stock.

00:01:48.080 --> 00:01:50.490
I will also be getting the short end of the stick.

00:01:51.470 --> 00:01:55.230
Tatsumi Takeshi. I'll curse you for life if you lose.

00:01:56.640 --> 00:02:01.260
Anyway, I want the three of them to be concentrating when they are playing!

00:02:01.920 --> 00:02:04.190
That is what I brought you to Japan for!

00:03:59.620 --> 00:04:03.700
Managing in Japan has been tough for you, isn't it?

00:04:05.050 --> 00:04:10.880
It's unexpected that after making such powerful statements, you would proceed to lose five in a row.

00:04:13.120 --> 00:04:17.710
Oh, please don't misunderstand. This is my unique way of encouragement.

00:04:18.940 --> 00:04:23.510
Thanks for your concern, Mr "Weird Hair" Fuwa.

00:04:24.690 --> 00:04:25.980
But it's okay.

00:04:27.610 --> 00:04:30.030
For we will be the victors today.

00:04:40.070 --> 00:04:44.010
We've really came to Nagoya.

00:04:45.640 --> 00:04:47.480
You guys have got to win today!

00:04:47.680 --> 00:04:48.800
That's right!

00:04:49.810 --> 00:04:53.880
We lost against FC Sapporo. And I got screamed at by my wife the moment I reached home.

00:04:54.030 --> 00:04:58.590
"Did you cheer for the team? Or have you gone for a walk instead?"

00:04:58.730 --> 00:05:02.060
I got lectured by my son right after that.

00:05:02.700 --> 00:05:04.300
I'm about the same as you too.

00:05:04.730 --> 00:05:05.710
Same here.

00:05:05.880 --> 00:05:06.890
Me too.

00:05:09.640 --> 00:05:10.990
What happened?

00:05:11.390 --> 00:05:13.600
Those guys are unusually quiet today.

00:05:15.160 --> 00:05:18.230
It seems that they created a ruckus in front of the team bus right after the previous game.

00:05:18.400 --> 00:05:21.240
It would be no surprise that they would do such a thing.

00:05:21.610 --> 00:05:25.120
If that's true, then it's a real disgrace.

00:05:29.340 --> 00:05:35.340
Once we return to Tokyo, we'll round up the old fans and reform our group!

00:05:36.310 --> 00:05:40.130
For this, we'll first need a victory! Let's cheer our hearts out!

00:06:11.080 --> 00:06:14.040
Those three Brazilians look real formidable.

00:06:15.240 --> 00:06:17.970
If we play right into their hands, we're dead.

00:06:18.260 --> 00:06:20.670
Don't you go around committing fouls in the danger area again.

00:06:21.160 --> 00:06:23.480
You're so stuck up, Akasaki!

00:06:23.800 --> 00:06:25.400
And you're still two years younger than me!

00:06:28.680 --> 00:06:32.180
So that guy's Pepe? Just you wait!

00:06:32.750 --> 00:06:37.060
Have you forgotten our plan, Kuro? I'm the one marking him.

00:06:37.520 --> 00:06:40.420
Sugie is obviously better than you in man-to-man marking.

00:06:40.500 --> 00:06:45.180
I know that! There's no harm in having a bit of vigilance, right?

00:06:45.470 --> 00:06:48.660
I will still need to help depending on the circumstances!

00:06:51.180 --> 00:06:52.480
Koshi.

00:06:54.920 --> 00:06:56.320
Isn't this better?

00:06:57.070 --> 00:07:00.290
I don't really dislike things like fate and hatred.

00:07:00.970 --> 00:07:03.470
Don't these things make the film more interesting?

00:07:04.760 --> 00:07:07.840
I don't know what you're trying to say, Gino.

00:07:08.180 --> 00:07:09.300
I don't have any hatred towards Fuwa.

00:07:13.000 --> 00:07:14.840
What I'm trying to say is...

00:07:16.420 --> 00:07:18.340
Let's win this game.

00:07:31.430 --> 00:07:34.220
Let's hit the ground running! Let's go!

00:07:51.070 --> 00:07:56.730
I initially wanted to have a word with Tatsumi, but I got to see a gutsy Gotou instead.

00:07:57.990 --> 00:08:06.400
Presently, nothing has changed. Though I did tell them that if they were to lose today, they are to resign.

00:08:10.220 --> 00:08:15.300
The one who left ETU in the lurch is him.

00:08:15.790 --> 00:08:19.520
That said though, the players are still diligently preparing for this.

00:08:22.420 --> 00:08:24.890
That is why we still need to back them up!

00:08:30.460 --> 00:08:31.890
Alright, let's do it!

00:08:41.860 --> 00:08:43.550
What's with that deafening cheer?

00:08:48.630 --> 00:08:50.010
I can't lose to them!

00:09:03.360 --> 00:09:07.060
Japanese people sure are an anxious bunch.

00:09:08.730 --> 00:09:10.680
The match has only just started.

00:09:14.120 --> 00:09:19.580
I see. The team is on a losing streak. They must be struggling right now.

00:09:30.140 --> 00:09:33.440
What's with those guys? The match has already started!

00:09:34.390 --> 00:09:36.060
Stop screwing around!

00:09:37.950 --> 00:09:40.100
Keep you focus, lads. Concentrate.

00:09:40.480 --> 00:09:42.540
Don't get mesmerized by the opponent's tempo.

00:09:43.640 --> 00:09:46.310
They will only show their ruthlessness for a brief moment.

00:09:57.900 --> 00:09:59.370
H-Here they come!

00:10:00.770 --> 00:10:04.020
That's fine with me! Show me what you've got!

00:10:06.890 --> 00:10:08.150
It's Zelberto!

00:10:18.550 --> 00:10:19.880
That's bad.

00:10:25.230 --> 00:10:26.410
Pepe's gone!

00:10:31.260 --> 00:10:32.210
It's Pepe!

00:10:33.270 --> 00:10:34.210
He's coming!

00:10:37.380 --> 00:10:38.670
He's gonna shoot!

00:10:48.690 --> 00:10:49.690
Offside?!

00:10:49.690 --> 00:10:51.130
That was scary!

00:10:54.460 --> 00:10:55.750
That was so close!

00:10:56.420 --> 00:10:58.380
That's a shame.

00:10:58.670 --> 00:11:02.010
It's okay, we're able to link up well right from the start.

00:11:02.590 --> 00:11:05.430
We should be able to enjoy ourselves more against this team.

00:11:06.930 --> 00:11:10.940
Pepe, I know you're unhappy, just get back here!

00:11:10.950 --> 00:11:13.690
Or the referee will give you a card!

00:11:14.930 --> 00:11:20.300
They sure made us worry when they clicked.

00:11:20.350 --> 00:11:22.510
You're too soft, Macchan.

00:11:23.800 --> 00:11:27.530
You're pathetic. Just calm down a little.

00:11:28.130 --> 00:11:30.660
Even the lads out there seem calmer than you.

00:11:30.920 --> 00:11:33.190
I don't want to hear that from you.

00:11:34.020 --> 00:11:39.190
I know very well that the three Brazilians not only possess technique, but speed as well.

00:11:39.820 --> 00:11:42.090
They also link up well with the whole team.

00:11:43.030 --> 00:11:46.790
Take the last few minutes for instance. I feel that this will continue to happen.

00:11:48.030 --> 00:11:52.130
Though that may be the case, it might not be a one-sided game. This is football after all.

00:11:54.200 --> 00:11:54.830
Sugie!

00:11:59.800 --> 00:12:02.010
That's it, Sugie! Keep him out!

00:12:02.120 --> 00:12:03.100
Hey, Pepe!

00:12:04.620 --> 00:12:07.460
Not bad, Kiyokawa! Nice cover!

00:12:09.450 --> 00:12:17.200
They are pumped. He was still so full of himself, and I thought he came up with something special.

00:12:18.260 --> 00:12:22.080
In the end, the Brazilians still ran circles around them.

00:12:23.860 --> 00:12:25.550
Tatsumi...

00:12:27.590 --> 00:12:30.980
How long can ETU hold out, I wonder?

00:12:32.760 --> 00:12:37.120
We never planned to play soccer with only three players.

00:12:56.960 --> 00:13:02.040
The midfielders are playing well, though the attack stops at Pepe.

00:13:04.850 --> 00:13:10.570
That centre-back sure is capable. If only we can make him commit a foul...

00:13:11.050 --> 00:13:12.120
Zelberto!

00:13:16.940 --> 00:13:18.650
Great run there!

00:13:22.420 --> 00:13:23.830
Nice, Koshi.

00:13:24.630 --> 00:13:26.930
I was just thinking it's about time.

00:13:28.020 --> 00:13:32.150
If we still don't attack now, the crowd will start to get bored.

00:13:32.270 --> 00:13:33.900
Good, Prince! Go!

00:13:39.070 --> 00:13:39.880
Nice!

00:13:40.080 --> 00:13:41.080
Great!

00:13:41.660 --> 00:13:43.120
Attack, ETU!

00:13:44.580 --> 00:13:46.080
Akasaki!

00:13:50.900 --> 00:13:51.850
Tsubaki!

00:13:54.200 --> 00:13:55.290
A chance!

00:13:55.610 --> 00:13:56.670
Go, Tsubaki!

00:14:04.970 --> 00:14:06.320
Foul, foul!

00:14:06.580 --> 00:14:10.420
My... the people who lives in a samba-loving country sure has strong legs!

00:14:10.780 --> 00:14:12.240
Beautiful, Carlos!

00:14:12.620 --> 00:14:14.330
Pass me the ball!

00:14:14.760 --> 00:14:15.420
Hi!

00:14:16.740 --> 00:14:17.570
Carlos!

00:14:18.920 --> 00:14:20.420
Not bad.

00:14:20.830 --> 00:14:22.710
Continue dribbling!

00:14:23.860 --> 00:14:27.450
I was hoping that they would teach me the Bossa Nova which someone recommended.

00:14:27.450 --> 00:14:30.860
Defend, defend! They're attacking!

00:14:32.960 --> 00:14:34.540
That's bad!

00:14:34.800 --> 00:14:36.120
Stop him, Ishiyama!

00:14:41.660 --> 00:14:44.640
They passed to Zelberto! Take note of Pepe!

00:14:54.140 --> 00:14:55.410
It's not Pepe!

00:14:56.440 --> 00:14:57.730
That's right.

00:14:59.570 --> 00:15:00.860
That's the one...

00:15:03.590 --> 00:15:08.040
Everybody's calling for Pepe. It's so annoying!

00:15:08.470 --> 00:15:10.820
Damn, he's gonna shoot!

00:15:12.550 --> 00:15:17.200
Open your eyes big! This is my shot at full speed!

00:15:23.170 --> 00:15:25.410
Nice, Kuro! You got there on time!

00:15:25.610 --> 00:15:28.080
That was close.

00:15:28.370 --> 00:15:30.630
We conceded a corner.

00:15:34.340 --> 00:15:39.680
Don't get in my way, Kuroda! I have no time to play with the likes of you.

00:15:40.390 --> 00:15:46.280
What are you saying, Itagaki? You're not even worth my effort!

00:15:55.320 --> 00:16:01.750
Why is that bastard marking me? ETU's best defender should be Sugie!

00:16:03.130 --> 00:16:07.120
I was always marked by Sugie whenever our teams met!

00:16:07.440 --> 00:16:10.080
How dare they change strategies just because of Pepe?

00:16:12.120 --> 00:16:14.070
Nagoya's ace is me!

00:16:15.270 --> 00:16:17.510
Stop underestimating me, ETU!

00:16:19.180 --> 00:16:26.790
From the looks of our formation, I should be the one marking Pepe. Why must I be the one taking on a second-fiddle?

00:16:29.460 --> 00:16:32.040
Stop screwing with me, Tatsumi you bastard!

00:16:34.220 --> 00:16:36.980
This guy isn't worthy to be my opponent!

00:16:44.730 --> 00:16:46.050
That was close.

00:16:46.220 --> 00:16:49.580
Alright! Let's slowly get the ball out!

00:17:03.070 --> 00:17:05.970
We're always getting into difficult situations.

00:17:07.610 --> 00:17:09.560
Is it okay to keep getting dominated?

00:17:13.520 --> 00:17:14.670
Because the defense is pushing up,

00:17:15.050 --> 00:17:19.810
The midfield space available to the opponent is restricted.

00:17:20.330 --> 00:17:23.540
Zelberto should be finding it hard to play his usual game.

00:17:26.130 --> 00:17:33.330
Still, our defense... Kuroda is influenced by Pepe's presence and is relaxing his mark on Itagaki.

00:17:35.830 --> 00:17:37.900
Itagaki possesses great speed.

00:17:39.850 --> 00:17:42.860
It will be troublesome if he continues getting chances like that.

00:17:43.700 --> 00:17:44.900
That's a worrying sign.

00:17:45.820 --> 00:17:49.750
Yes. If only Kuroda would stop underestimating him.

00:17:52.840 --> 00:17:54.760
Great defending!

00:17:56.560 --> 00:17:59.510
Though I would like to initiate an attack with Pepe, he's closely guarded by No.3.

00:18:00.810 --> 00:18:07.780
Still, the fun of football is to keep on passing.

00:18:15.070 --> 00:18:16.800
Just like this.

00:18:18.610 --> 00:18:21.390
They came from behind. No offside!

00:18:21.760 --> 00:18:23.080
I thought I got it covered?!

00:18:24.890 --> 00:18:26.470
Great pass, Brazilian bastard.

00:18:27.590 --> 00:18:29.570
I'll show you the abilities of a Japanese!

00:18:29.860 --> 00:18:30.980
You asshole!

00:18:31.900 --> 00:18:34.170
Catch me if you can, birdbrain!

00:18:34.970 --> 00:18:36.690
I'll show you my shooting...

00:18:37.950 --> 00:18:39.190
...from this angle!

00:18:39.360 --> 00:18:40.050
Shoot!

00:18:43.290 --> 00:18:46.600
You saw that coming long ago?! Great work, Kuroda!

00:18:48.260 --> 00:18:49.580
Nice!

00:18:49.580 --> 00:18:51.420
That's great, Kuroda!

00:19:09.450 --> 00:19:12.000
Alright, alright! Ok, ok!

00:19:16.250 --> 00:19:20.160
What in the world happened to ETU? They're just defending.

00:19:33.990 --> 00:19:35.290
Nice one, Kuroda!

00:19:35.520 --> 00:19:37.320
You've completely contained Itagaki!

00:19:37.700 --> 00:19:39.050
Though you're always late!

00:19:39.530 --> 00:19:42.060
Wasn't that a foul?!

00:19:42.460 --> 00:19:45.280
So you were looking for a foul.

00:19:45.960 --> 00:19:47.970
You've stooped real low for a striker.

00:19:48.230 --> 00:19:51.530
What are you saying, you bastard! You were the one playing all rough!

00:19:51.820 --> 00:19:55.010
Keep on barking, you dog.

00:19:56.040 --> 00:19:59.950
I'll never let you pass me! You're not even worth my effort, Itagaki!

00:20:02.190 --> 00:20:03.990
Kuroda!

00:20:05.430 --> 00:20:07.730
That Kuroda is on a roll.

00:20:07.960 --> 00:20:11.400
He managed to stop their attacks at the most crucial of times.

00:20:11.830 --> 00:20:19.150
Sugie is marking Pepe, which is why he couldn't assist the team. Initially, i was worried about their stability.

00:20:20.360 --> 00:20:22.510
What? That's how you feel?

00:20:25.040 --> 00:20:27.990
I think Kuroda is quite reliable though.

00:20:30.690 --> 00:20:32.010
Throw everything at us!

00:20:32.930 --> 00:20:34.220
But it's Kuroda, you know?

00:20:34.510 --> 00:20:36.320
Yeah, I know.

00:20:37.380 --> 00:20:40.860
If his opponent's Itagaki, Kuroda will win it.

00:20:42.460 --> 00:20:46.110
Itagaki has been playing as a right-sided striker until last season, right?

00:20:47.090 --> 00:20:51.910
During the game against ETU, he scored 2 goals too. The one marking him was also Kuroda.

00:20:53.370 --> 00:20:57.990
Itagaki might have thought that Kuroda's not his match.

00:20:58.800 --> 00:21:01.350
But in reality, not once was Itagaki able to get past Kuroda's defending.

00:21:03.100 --> 00:21:05.980
I dug through a pile of past game statistics and realized that...

00:21:06.230 --> 00:21:11.170
Itagaki's goals came either from a follow-up or an exploitation of space.

00:21:14.330 --> 00:21:17.460
Itagaki's strengths; slipping past the backline...

00:21:18.380 --> 00:21:23.030
...and one-on-one techniques totally failed against Kuroda.

00:21:23.110 --> 00:21:28.540
Now that you've mentioned it, it does seem that way. But why?

00:21:29.290 --> 00:21:30.200
Who knows?

00:21:30.780 --> 00:21:32.200
Probably because they complement each other.

00:21:32.850 --> 00:21:34.880
They do look similar.

00:21:35.540 --> 00:21:37.550
So he based it on that?

00:21:38.440 --> 00:21:43.700
Additionally, with Pepe's addition, Itagaki got chucked into his unfamiliar left side.

00:21:44.930 --> 00:21:49.180
If Kuroda is able to mark him out, Itagaki is practically useless.

00:21:56.620 --> 00:21:59.720
Not yet. It's still not the time to leave my position.

00:22:02.590 --> 00:22:06.230
Just a little bit more... Keep it there.

00:22:07.700 --> 00:22:08.560
Now!

00:22:10.740 --> 00:22:11.800
See that?

00:22:18.000 --> 00:22:21.100
That's a pity. Still, not bad, Itagaki!

00:22:38.440 --> 00:22:39.390
Sera!

00:22:43.300 --> 00:22:44.650
Are you alright?

00:22:45.190 --> 00:22:46.450
Did you hurt your back, Sera?

00:24:14.990 --> 00:24:17.630
Remind yourself why I've decided to choose you.

00:24:17.980 --> 00:24:20.070
Get past me if you can, dumbass!

00:24:21.390 --> 00:24:22.230
Come on!

00:24:22.480 --> 00:24:23.690
They're attacking up the flanks!

00:24:23.970 --> 00:24:25.550
Stick to him, Ishiyama!

00:24:25.560 --> 00:24:28.020
Make them cower in fear!
